                <pb facs="1138" n="1058" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1058"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bowen to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 85.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward some memoranda
                    in regard to the firing upon of the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Viking</hi>.
                    These documents were filed with me by the managing director of the New York and
                    Bermudez Company, Mr. Rake.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert W. Bowen.</hi></signed></closer>





